{
  "A native `<button>` drawn from the design tokens: three variants, three tones, three sizes, an icon, an `&` access key. It can be a toggle, show that work is running, and open a menu or any content — from the whole button, or with `split` from an arrow next to it while the button keeps its own action.": "",
  "Both ways are complete. Every prop takes a value or a function; a function of a reactive object keeps the button in step with it. A property set programmatically takes the same.": "",
  "Variants, tones, sizes": "",
  "`solid` buttons are pressable: an opaque fill, a bottom edge, a highlight along the top and a small move when pressed. `outline` has a frame, `ghost` shows only on hover. The tone picks the colors; the size the height, from the density tokens (switch Compact above).": "",
  "Text, icon, children": "",
  "`text` is the caption; JSX children come after it. `icon` takes an image address or any element or component, before the text or after it (`iconPosition`). A button with only an icon needs a name: give it a `hint`.": "",
  "Toggle": "",
  "With `toggle` a click turns `pressed` on and off; `x-model` binds it two-way.": "",
  "Busy": "",
  "While `busy`, a spinner shows over the content, presses are ignored and the size does not change. The text stays for screen readers, with `aria-busy`.": "",
  "Disabled": "",
  "A disabled button is natively disabled: it leaves the Tab order and cannot be pressed. With `focusableWhenDisabled` it keeps its place and only gets `aria-disabled`, so a keyboard or screen reader user can still find it — and a hint can say why it is off.": "",
  "With `menu` the whole button opens a list of commands. Items can have an icon, a check mark, a group line, be disabled or hidden; each `&` key chooses its item while the menu is open. An item field may be a function: the open menu follows what it reads.": "",
  "Split": "",
  "With `split` the button keeps its own action (`onclick`) and an arrow next to it opens the menu. The two are separate Tab stops; Alt+Down on the button opens the menu too. `split` can change at any time; a menu itself (`split`, `menu` or `dropDown`) must be there when the button is created, since it makes the button two parts.": "",
  "`dropDown` opens any component instead of a menu: a picker, a small form. Focus goes to its first field; Escape or a press outside closes it.": "",
  "Press the button. With a menu and no `split`: open the menu, focus on its first item.": "",
  "Press it (Control + Option + key on Apple platforms).": "",
  "On a button that opens a menu (or on the arrow of a split button): open it, focus on the first / last item.": "",
  "On the main part of a split button: open the menu.": "",
  "The next / previous item, wrapping around. Disabled items are reachable.": "",
  "The first / last item.": "",
  "The item whose `&` key it is is chosen; otherwise focus goes to the next item starting with it.": "",
  "Choose the focused item.": "",
  "Close the menu or drop-down; focus goes back to the part that opened it.": "",
  "Close the menu and go on to the next control.": "",
  "A native `<button>` (two with `split`: the button and the arrow), so forms, Enter, Space and screen readers work as they always do.": "",
  "The text, without the `&` marker. An icon-only button is named by its `hint` (or your `aria-label`). The arrow of a split button is named from `uiLocale` (\"More options\").": "",
  "`aria-busy=\"true\"`; the text stays readable under the spinner.": "",
  "`aria-haspopup=\"menu\"` and `aria-expanded` on the part that opens it; the list is `role=\"menu\"`, items `menuitem` or `menuitemcheckbox` with `aria-checked`, disabled items `aria-disabled`, group lines `separator`.": "",
  "`aria-haspopup=\"dialog\"`; the popup is `role=\"dialog\"`, named by the button's text. Focus goes to its first field.": "",
  "Only for keyboard use, the design system's double ring.": "",
  "The only text a button writes itself is the name of a split button's arrow. It comes from `uiLocale.strings`, which starts with the page's `lang` (English and Turkish ship) and can be set to any `UiStrings`; every button follows at once. The set is kept as it is given: to change one text, assign a new set (`uiLocale.strings = { ...uiLocale.strings, moreOptions: 'Mehr' }`); a text changed inside the set is not seen.": "",
  "The button (or the group of a button with a menu). `data-variant`, `data-tone`, `data-size`, `data-icon-position`, `data-stretch`, `data-pressed`, `data-busy`, `data-icon`, `data-mode=\"menu|split\"`.": "",
  "What is pressed: the button itself, or `.mx-button__main` and `.mx-button__arrow`.": "",
  "The icon, the arrow glyph of a menu button, the busy spinner.": "",
  "The surface the menu opens on (`data-side=\"bottom|top\"`).": "",
  "The menu, its items, its group lines.": "",
  "Unit: what is pressed, with its frame (the bottom side is a key’s edge), its fill and state layer (`image`) and its focus ring (outline and `glow`). Each look is a state (`accent`, `danger`, `outline`, `outline-accent`, `ghost`, …), and each look in each state too (`hover`, `toggled-hover`, `open`, `pressed`, `focus`, `toggled`, `disabled`: `outline-hover`, `accent-pressed`, …); also `icon-only`, `busy`, and a split button’s `main` and `arrow`.": "",
  "Units: the icon, the text, the arrow of a menu (`open`), the busy spinner and the line of a split button, each look a state.": "",
  "How far a solid button moves when pressed, a square icon button, the caption’s line box, the spinner’s turn.": "",
  "The popup surface and the menu items.": "",
  "All of them reference design-system tokens; see [Tokens](/tokens). Override one after `styles.css` to restyle every button.": "",
  "The caption. `&` marks the access key (`&Save` → Alt+S), `&&` is a literal `&`. JSX children come after it.": "",
  "`solid` (filled, pressable), `outline` (a frame), `ghost` (only on hover).": "",
  "`standard`, `accent` (the main action), `danger` (a destructive one).": "",
  "`sm`, `md`, `lg`: the density tokens' control heights.": "",
  "An image address, or any element or component (an `<svg>` in JSX, an icon font tag). Decorative: hidden from screen readers.": "",
  "The icon before or after the text.": "",
  "The native type. `button` by default, so a button in a form never submits by accident.": "",
  "A tooltip (`title`). It also names a button that has only an icon.": "",
  "A toggle button: a click turns `pressed` on and off (`aria-pressed`).": "",
  "The state of a toggle button. `x-model` binds it two-way.": "",
  "Work is running: a spinner shows over the content, presses are ignored, the size stays, `aria-busy` is set.": "",
  "Disabled, it keeps its place in the Tab order with `aria-disabled`, so a screen reader finds it and reads it as dimmed.": "",
  "With a menu: the button keeps its own action and an arrow next to it opens the menu. Without it the whole button opens the menu.": "",
  "The commands of the menu, read each time it opens.": "",
  "Any content to open instead of a menu: a picker, a small form.": "",
  "Set programmatically with a value or a function, like the prop: `b.tone = () => this.state.tone` is followed, `b.tone = 'accent'` replaces it.": "",
  "`pressed`, for `x-model`.": "",
  "Whether the menu or drop-down is open; setting it opens or closes it.": "",
  "Whether it was created with `split`, `menu` or `dropDown`.": "",
  "Opens the menu or drop-down with focus on its first item; `false` when there is nothing to open, or it is disabled or busy.": "",
  "Closes it; focus inside goes back to the part that opened it.": "",
  "Your menu items may be plain or reactive; the button reads them as they are. After changing them in place, call `refresh()`. An open menu shows the change at once.": "",
  "Focuses the button (its main part with a menu).": "",
  "The DOM click of the button: its own action. With `split`, the arrow and the menu do not fire it; with a menu and no `split`, the click opens the menu.": "",
  "A menu item was chosen, after the item's own `click`. `e`: `{ item, source, event }`.": "",
  "MenuItem": "",
  "The label; `&` marks the key that chooses it while the menu is open.": "",
  "An icon; a function is called each time the item is drawn.": "",
  "`false`: shown dimmed, reachable, cannot be chosen.": "",
  "`false`: left out.": "",
  "Given, the item is a `menuitemcheckbox` and shows a check mark when `true`. Flip it in its `click`.": "",
  "function": "",
  "Runs when it is chosen, after the menu closed.": "",
  "The app's own value.": "",
  "The menu and the surface it opens on are shared parts, `MenuList` and `Popup`, exported for other components to use.": ""
}
